# One row per fixture: <name> <patch> <repatch> <round trip>.
#
# CHANGED means the patch exits 0 and the file differs. REFUSED means it exits
# non-zero and the file is untouched. NOOP is a zero exit over an unchanged
# file, which only an already patched module may report. LIVE is a zero exit
# that left a live call in the module, which no row may name. The check reads
# a call on one line and a mode that leads its own continuation line.
#
# IDEMPOTENT means a second patch over the same file exits 0 and moves nothing.
# FAILED is a refusal, which is what breaks a repeated patch.
#
# IDENTITY means the un-patch restores the fixture byte for byte. Every
# fixture but the refusals and the already patched ones moves the file, so no
# row earns its verdict by doing nothing. UNPATCH_FAILED is an un-patch that
# refused, which is what a module carrying no marked call reports.
